@page "/"

<PageTitle>Day 3 Demo - State Challenges</PageTitle>

<h1>Day 3 Demo: State Challenges</h1>

<p class="lead">
    This demo shows the <strong>state-loss problem</strong> in Blazor.
    Each page stores cart data in its own private field. Navigate between
    Products and Cart to see what happens.
</p>

<div class="card mt-3">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h5 class="card-title">Try This</h5>
        <ol>
            <li>Go to <strong>Products</strong> and add a few items to the cart.</li>
            <li>Note the cart count at the bottom of the Products page.</li>
            <li>Click <strong>Shopping Cart</strong> in the sidebar.</li>
            <li>Is the cart empty or populated?</li>
            <li>Navigate back to <strong>Products</strong>. Are your items still there?</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="text-muted mb-0">
            This is the state-loss problem that the Flux/Redux pattern solves.
            Each component has independent state that does not survive navigation.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
